    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter June 9th with two clear offensive pillars. **Yordan Alvarez** (81.25) and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (80.98) headline our lineup, both positioned in elite tiers due to highly favorable matchups. **Yordan Alvarez** benefits from a high-efficiency pairing against Ure\u00f1a, while **Pete Crow-Armstrong** leverages a massive 33% combined boost from park factors and a plus-matchup against Sugano. Given our league\u2019s aggressive valuation of sprint speed, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** is a foundational start today; his ability to impact the scarcest category (SB) while maintaining an 80+ efficiency score makes him arguably our most important asset in the 5x5 Roto context. **Christian Yelich** also earns a strong recommendation (68.09) as we project him into the leadoff spot against Ginn, where he gains significant value from the platoon advantage.\n\nConversely, we are treading carefully with our corner infielders and middle-order bats. **Kazuma Okamoto** (40.13) and **Dillon Dingler** (43.02) remain in the lineup but are hovering dangerously close to the Zebras' 40.0 benchmark. Both are stifled by tough pitching matchups, specifically against Wheeler and Bradley, respectively. The most difficult personnel decision involved **Chase Meidroth**, who logged a 47.99 score. While his efficiency outperformed several starters, he was ultimately benched because his absolute ceiling is capped compared to the multi-category upside of players like **Caleb Durbin**\u2014who, despite a slight park penalty, remains vital for our SB totals against Martinez. \n\nRisk management is central to today\u2019s deployment. We are navigating significant headwinds for **Trea Turner** (52.43) and **Kyle Schwarber** (51.64), both of whom are facing Cease; the elite skill of the opposing arm has cratered their base projections. Furthermore, the lineup status for **Gary Sanchez** and **Christian Yelich** remains \"pending,\" necessitating a late-afternoon check. We have opted to bench **Casey Schmitt** (39.84) entirely, as his sub-40 efficiency score against Alvarez represents an unacceptable risk to our daily game caps.",
